I don't see the same balance point you do. I find when I play the game
straight up, my characters usually get overmatched by the opposition.
I then find I have to armor up more heavily to compensate. This creates
burden which is a bad thing.

I find that the protection AC gives better balance to my characters
as they level up. The buff pet definitely helps too.

The protection racket isn't about the XL1. It isn't the critical
component. The additional weightless AC is the critical component because
once your AC is negative each hit (which is reduced to a 5% chance) has
some of its damage mitigated. Simply put you can sustain a lot more
attacks with a neagtive AC than otherwise.

Protection makes it easier to get into negative AC territory without
having to wear stuff. Eventually that function is taken over by
enchant armor and whatever protection your god decides to bestow upon
you. But in the early game before you've come across a ton of ?oEA or
an altar you can pray on, Minetown protection is the next best thing.

I think that diving for Minetown is ill advised. But if you take the time to
armor up, gather your money/stuff from the Dlvl 2-5 shops, buff the pet, and
bump up your HP, then make protection your first target at a low XL is
a reasonable goal.

